<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moktar Ould Daddah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1924">1924</a>–<a href="/years/2003">2003</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Moktar Ould Daddah was the first president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritania">Mauritania</a>, from independence on 28 November 1960 until 1978. A lawyer trained in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, he became head of government in 1957, oversaw the building of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nouakchott">Nouakchott</a> as the new capital and later made his People's Party the sole legal party. The costly war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-sahara">Western Sahara</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polisario-front">Polisario Front</a> led to his overthrow by a military coup in July 1978.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moktar-ould-daddah.jpg" alt="Moktar Ould Daddah" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moktar_Ould_Daddah.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
